  "notes": "Used for both literal physical falls (sense 1) and figurative decline (sense 2). The physical sense often appears in news reports about accidents.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {転落|てんらく}{事故|じこ} — falling accident\n- {転落|てんらく}{死|し} — death from a fall\n- {転落|てんらく}{防止|ぼうし} — fall prevention\n- {転落|てんらく}{人生|じんせい} — a life in decline\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {落下|らっか} — falling (of objects, more neutral/scientific)\n- {墜落|ついらく} — crash (specifically aircraft or from great height)\n- {没落|ぼつらく} — ruin, downfall (only figurative, especially of families or aristocracy)",
